      "claimKind": "unclassified",
      "headingCount": 14,
      "unheadedBlockCount": 32,
      "mixedFileBlockCount": 0,
      "headings": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "text": "Why a single `done` status split into delivered → retrospective → cleanup → done",
          "anchor": "why-a-single-done-status-split-into-delivered-retrospective-cleanup-done",
          "githubAnchor": "why-a-single-done-status-split-into-delivered-retrospective-cleanup-done",
          "stableAnchor": "h-4d185dbed052"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The conflation this replaced",
          "anchor": "the-conflation-this-replaced",
          "githubAnchor": "the-conflation-this-replaced",
          "stableAnchor": "h-16d64ba605bd"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The four statuses, and what each one actually gates",
          "anchor": "the-four-statuses-and-what-each-one-actually-gates",
          "githubAnchor": "the-four-statuses-and-what-each-one-actually-gates",
          "stableAnchor": "h-fca4ecb90744"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Where the two old gates actually moved",
          "anchor": "where-the-two-old-gates-actually-moved",
          "githubAnchor": "where-the-two-old-gates-actually-moved",
          "stableAnchor": "h-02cd375e7016"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Why `cleanup`'s TTL delay is deliberate, not laziness",
          "anchor": "why-cleanups-ttl-delay-is-deliberate-not-laziness",
          "githubAnchor": "why-cleanups-ttl-delay-is-deliberate-not-laziness",
          "stableAnchor": "h-73f70d54ebb2"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The dependent-opens-early tradeoff, and why it isn't a new risk",
          "anchor": "the-dependent-opens-early-tradeoff-and-why-it-isnt-a-new-risk",
          "githubAnchor": "the-dependent-opens-early-tradeoff-and-why-it-isnt-a-new-risk",
          "stableAnchor": "h-1a8dd326f7d7"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What `retrospective` becoming a status (not a stage) actually retired",
          "anchor": "what-retrospective-becoming-a-status-not-a-stage-actually-retired",
          "githubAnchor": "what-retrospective-becoming-a-status-not-a-stage-actually-retired",
          "stableAnchor": "h-d9bad68f3722"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Two places the same underlying set had to expand — and one place it deliberately didn't",
          "anchor": "two-places-the-same-underlying-set-had-to-expand-and-one-place-it-deliberately-didnt",
          "githubAnchor": "two-places-the-same-underlying-set-had-to-expand-and-one-place-it-deliberately-didnt",
          "stableAnchor": "h-e9439f680e5e"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "No backfill — old `done` items keep their real (incomplete) history",
          "anchor": "no-backfill-old-done-items-keep-their-real-incomplete-history",
          "githubAnchor": "no-backfill-old-done-items-keep-their-real-incomplete-history",
          "stableAnchor": "h-48045c529ce1"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Outcome",
          "anchor": "outcome",
          "githubAnchor": "outcome",
          "stableAnchor": "h-5f81aa7d293e"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The implementation drifted from D7/D8 in two places — a real, evidenced bug, not a design flaw",
          "anchor": "the-implementation-drifted-from-d7d8-in-two-places-a-real-evidenced-bug-not-a-design-flaw",
          "githubAnchor": "the-implementation-drifted-from-d7d8-in-two-places-a-real-evidenced-bug-not-a-design-flaw",
          "stableAnchor": "h-1f0e5e1102a8"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The chain's real blind spot: nothing detects an item forgotten mid-chain, because nothing needs to",
          "anchor": "the-chains-real-blind-spot-nothing-detects-an-item-forgotten-mid-chain-because-nothing-needs-to",
          "githubAnchor": "the-chains-real-blind-spot-nothing-detects-an-item-forgotten-mid-chain-because-nothing-needs-to",
          "stableAnchor": "h-28dea9c48d15"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "A tempting simplification — merging the two loops — was explicitly rejected, twice",
          "anchor": "a-tempting-simplification-merging-the-two-loops-was-explicitly-rejected-twice",
          "githubAnchor": "a-tempting-simplification-merging-the-two-loops-was-explicitly-rejected-twice",
          "stableAnchor": "h-58ce8263d229"
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "text": "The domain-agnostic guarantee (D5) got its own regression-proving child task",
          "anchor": "the-domain-agnostic-guarantee-d5-got-its-own-regression-proving-child-task",
          "githubAnchor": "the-domain-agnostic-guarantee-d5-got-its-own-regression-proving-child-task",
          "stableAnchor": "h-0e774c1dcf60"
        }
      ],
